# CasaNova monorepo — what stays out of history, and why.
# Written against the actual tree, not a template. Each block names its reason.

# ── Build outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make package` materialises ~10 GB of staged trees and update tarballs
# here; all of it regenerates from source.
/build/

# Compiled service binaries dropped at module roots by `go build`.
/CasaNova/CasaNova
/CasaNova/casanova
/CasaNova-Gateway/CasaNova-Gateway
/CasaNova-Gateway/casanova-gateway
/CasaNova-MessageBus/CasaNova-MessageBus
/CasaNova-MessageBus/casanova-message-bus
/CasaNova-AppManagement/CasaNova-AppManagement
/CasaNova-AppManagement/casanova-app-management
/CasaNova-UserService/CasaNova-UserService
/CasaNova-UserService/casanova-user-service
/CasaNova-LocalStorage/CasaNova-LocalStorage
/CasaNova-LocalStorage/casanova-local-storage
/CasaNova-JobManagement/CasaNova-JobManagement
/CasaNova-JobManagement/casanova-job-management
/CasaNova-Virt/CasaNova-Virt
/CasaNova-Virt/casanova-virt
/CasaNova-Driver/CasaNova-Driver
/CasaNova-Driver/casanova-driver
/CasaNova-CLI/CasaNova-CLI
/CasaNova-CLI/casanova-cli

# Frontend dependency and build output.
/CasaNova-UI-v2/node_modules/
/CasaNova-UI-v2/dist/

# ── Reference material, not project source ───────────────────────────
# GIFTABLES: an extracted ZimaOS image kept as wire-format ground truth
# (5.7 GB of a third party's binaries — provenance, not our code).
/GIFTABLES/

# LEGACY: third-party projects kept for reading (Cosmos, the v1 UI, …).
# Their licenses and history are their own; they do not belong in ours.
/LEGACY/
/portainer-develop/

# CasaNova-AppLibrary is a sibling project with its own upstream history
# and release cycle (app catalog, fork of CasaOS-AppStore). It remains an
# independent repository beside this one.
/CasaNova-AppLibrary/

# Upstream CasaOS git histories of the forked modules, preserved on disk
# for archaeology after the monorepo flattened them. See
# docs/engineering/repository-baseline.md.
/.upstream-git-archive/

# ── Local state, machine-specific, or secret-bearing ─────────────────
# Operator handoff notes and session-context archives: they contain live
# credentials and full working transcripts. Operational material, never
# history. (The 86 MB context tarball in here is also the only copy.)
/docs/handoff/

# Local agent/tooling state (root and nested); the permission list embeds
# local commands and the launch config is machine-specific.
.claude/

# Per-machine frontend overrides (the LAN backend URL of one dev box).
/CasaNova-UI-v2/.env.local

# ── Ephemera ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Assistant-harness skill definitions (session tooling, not project source).
/.agents/
